Title: Judge's X Word Puzzle No. 10
Author: Mrs. Ruth Helffrich
Date: 1927-07-02
Byline: Submitted by Mrs. Ruth Helffrich, Bath, Pa. Judge pays $25 for each puzzle printed.
Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-07-02_93/page/n31/mode/1up
Number: 10
Solution-Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-07-09_93/page/n29/mode/1up


NEWT##SPA##GAIT
E#ION#TIN#ARC#I
WISP#CONGO#OMEN
SKEIN#LEO#SWEAT
#E#CAFE#REEL#R#
##U#MANDATE#S##
FALLEN#R#CROWDS
RITE#AWASH#DAIS
ARREST#N#IODINE
##A#LINKING#N##
#R#MICA#AGED#U#
DENIM#TOM#ERASE
OPEN#LIMBS#OVEN
O#ACT#VII#ONE#D
MARE##ETC##ERRS


A1. What is the name of a small tailed batrachian of lizard-like appearance? ~ NEWT
A4. What is a good destination for the water-wagon? ~ SPA
A7. Name something usually effected by too much use of Gordon Water. ~ GAIT
A10. Name a Greek poet who lived about 450 B. C. ~ ION
A11. What can be found in a Ford parked in a country lane on a moonlight night? ~ TIN
A12. What is always found in the best circles? ~ ARC
A13. What do corpulent ladies envy? ~ WISP
A15. Name a river in Africa. ~ CONGO
A16. What is an augury? ~ OMEN
A18. What does many a good yarn come in? ~ SKEIN
A20. Who is the King of Beasts? ~ LEO
A21. What is rarely ever the product of union labor? ~ SWEAT
A22. Name one kind of filling station. ~ CAFE
A24. What do Scotch best-steppers dance? ~ REEL
A27. Name something very commanding. ~ MANDATE
A30. What kind of arches are useless in bridge construction? ~ FALLEN
A33. What are seldom seen in church these days? ~ CROWDS
A37. What is a formal religious act? ~ RITE
A38. What was the condition of the Mississippi Valley this year? ~ AWASH
A39. What are the seats of the mighty placed upon? ~ DAIS
A40. What is apt to cause that pinched feeling? ~ ARREST
A42. Name a non-metallic element much used in medicine. ~ IODINE
A44. What common task are ministers, blacksmiths and jewelers often engaged in? ~ LINKING
A48. What silicate has a prismatic angle of 120 degrees? ~ MICA
A49. What would Methusela be, if he were still alive? ~ AGED
A52. From what material is overalls made? ~ DENIM
A54. What name comes first in a well-known trinity of boys? ~ TOM
A56. What should you do about your mistakes? ~ ERASE
A59. What should you do when opportunity knocks? ~ OPEN
A60. What can be found on all pear trees? ~ LIMBS
A61. Where should the half-baked be put? ~ OVEN
A62. What do Congressmen often pass? (not liquor). ~ ACT
A63. What is par in African Golf? (Roman numerals). ~ VII
A64. Name something singular. ~ ONE
A65. What is the name of the female of the equine mammal? ~ MARE
A66. What is an abbreviation for a Latin word meaning "and so forth"? ~ ETC
A67. What does many a man do when he gives a girl an engagement ring? ~ ERRS

D1. Name something it is difficult to find in the tabloids. ~ NEWS
D2. What kind of man is a bachelor? ~ WISE
D3. What is a subject for discourse? ~ TOPIC
D4. What kind of car is dangerous to drive? ~ STOLEN
D5. What is green all the year round? (not sophomore). ~ PINE
D6. What kind of cat wears a beautiful coat? ~ ANGORA
D7. What does a dog do when he's mad? ~ GROWL
D8. What is the highest point of anything? ~ ACME
D9. What is one way to give color? ~ TINT
D14. Who looks like Mike in the Funnies? ~ IKE
D17. Name a listening-in device. ~ EAR
D19. What does a convict lose for a number? ~ NAME
D21. Who is supposed to be a real wise guy? ~ SEER
D23. What kind of person is full of hot-dogmas? ~ FANATIC
D25. What does an artist do when he comes to the scratch? ~ ETCHING
D26. What adjective means "beyond due limit, extreme"? ~ ULTRA
D28. What did the Federal agent do to put down liquor? ~ DRANK
D29. What is the girl-friend's boy-friend? ~ SWAIN
D30. What is friar's title? ~ FRA
D31. What should saxophone players get? ~ AIR
D32. Name a well-beioved general in the Civil War. ~ LEE
D34. What do they call a person who is crazy—but rich? ~ ODD
D35. What part of the dinner does the jazz orchestra supply? ~ DIN
D36. Name a point on the compass. ~ SSE
D41. What kind of girls are unpopular in Turkey? ~ SLIM
D43. What is the reverse or S shaped curve used in ornamental construction? ~ OGEE
D45. What is the only kind of person hard to find in New York City? ~ NATIVE
D46. What kind of English poetry is most prevalent? ~ IAMBIC
D47. What is a dress fabric having a corded appearance? ~ REP
D48. What means "to cut or chop into small bits"? ~ MINCE
D50. What is the male who never works? ~ DRONE
D51. What makes a car second-hand? ~ USE
D52. What is hopeless? ~ DOOM
D53. Where does the bald-headed row want to be? ~ NEAR
D55. What means "to leave out"? ~ OMIT
D57. What is it "to declare positively"? ~ AVER
D58. What is supposed to meet with a hoop-snake? ~ ENDS


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
A49: What would Methusela be, if he were still alive? → Methuselah
D30: What is friar's title? → What is a friar's title?
D32: Name a well-beioved general in the Civil War. → beloved

